      "payload": {
        "content": "When evaluating experimental design, flag reliance on single, simple datasets (e.g., MNIST) as a weakness for generalizability and request expansion to complex benchmarks (e.g., CIFAR-10, ImageNet). Scrutinize reproducibility by checking for missing hyperparameters, random seeds, and code availability; require detailed appendices for independent verification. Assess statistical rigor by identifying single-run results without confidence intervals or significance tests, and mandate reporting of mean/variance over multiple independent runs. Evaluate comparisons to prior work by checking for missing state-of-the-art baselines or relevant architectural variants that could mitigate observed issues. Acknowledge valid methodological designs that effectively isolate specific trade-offs or phenomena, even if other aspects are weak.",
